WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.220
Evidence is the bridge between control claims and assessment conclusions.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.160
A cloud service provider may say a control is implemented, but the assessment process needs support for that statement.

3
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:28.460
Evidence can include policies, procedures, diagrams, implementation descriptions, configuration records, access review artifacts, logs, tickets, scan results, test results, incident records, risk decisions, and operational records.

4
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.720
The exact evidence depends on the control and system.

5
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.600
The cloud service provider is responsible for implementing and operating the service and for preparing evidence that accurately describes it.

6
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:49.260
An independent assessor, commonly discussed as a 3PAO at a high level, evaluates the system and produces evidence-based assessment results.

7
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:57.360
Agency reviewers and authorizing officials consider the package, findings, risk posture, and mission context.

8
00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.140
The roles are different, and good communication between them matters.

9
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.140
A Moderate assessment depends on consistency.

10
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.640
Documentation should match diagrams.

11
00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.460
Diagrams should match architecture.

12
00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.600
Architecture should match deployed configuration.

13
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.660
Policies should match procedures.

14
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.240
Procedures should match tickets and logs.

15
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:25.540
If the evidence story is inconsistent, reviewers may lose confidence even when the underlying control is partly present.

16
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.560
Consistency is one reason mature operations matter so much.

17
00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.080
Findings and remediation plans are normal parts of security work.

18
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.220
The goal is not to pretend there are no weaknesses.

19
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:45.960
The goal is to identify risk, assign ownership, plan remediation, track progress, and communicate honestly.

20
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:54.540
A strong provider treats assessment as a structured way to learn whether controls are effective, not as a performance where every answer must sound perfect.
